Subject: [PATCH] emacs: Archive notmuch mail by moving its file
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: tozlwyntmyxlllpmrvyltnmstypmzxsu

On this list a message is archived when its file lives under
maildir/archive/, and the post-new hook derives the archived and inbox
tags from that. notmuch-emacs only edits tags, so its "a" key did
nothing lasting: the next notmuch new put inbox back. Archiving took a
second step outside emacs to move the file.

Make the archived tag the operation. "a" now adds archived, and a tag
hook moves the file into archive/ at once and reindexes. C-u a removes
the tag and moves the file back to cur/. Any path that tags through
notmuch-emacs works the same way, whether "a" on a message, a thread
or a region, or "+" by hand.

The filesystem stays the source of truth. A draft never moves, and a
tag that matches no move is corrected by notmuch new, so the database
always agrees with what is committed to the mail branch.
