change-id: tozlwyntmyxlllpmrvyltnmstypmzxsu

This needs patch 1 of "[PATCH v2 0/2] Archive messages that need no
answer" [1], "notmuch: Tag messages under archive/ as archived" [2].
Without it, notmuch new puts inbox back on a moved message and never
drops archived from an unarchived one.

It supersedes "[PATCH v2] mail: Add just archive" [3] and both patches
of "[PATCH 0/2] Archive from notmuch-emacs with the archive tag" [4].
With no tag-then-script step, there is no archive request tag to keep
out of the inbox.

Files go flat into maildir/archive/, as in [3]. Unarchived files go to
cur/, since synchronize_flags is off and nothing reads the
subdirectory.

Tested in a scratch maildir with the real post-new hook, calling
notmuch-tag with notmuch-archive-tags as "a" and C-u a do. Archiving
moved files from cur/ and new/ into archive/ and left them tagged
archived only. A draft in the same query stayed put. Unarchiving moved
the file to cur/ and brought inbox back. An unrelated tag moved
nothing. just test fails in this jail, which lacks the markdown-mode
port: init.el stops at that require, before the notmuch settings.

